            <ArticleTitle>Carotidynia: magnetic resonance imaging and ultrasonographic imaging of a self-limiting disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>91-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00062-010-0042-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article describes the characteristic symptoms of carotidynia and the diagnostic options for this rare and not yet officially recognized disease entity. Based on a case report the findings of magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) and ultrasound scanning are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
